 "text": "9/29/26, 9:42 AM\n01(05) = periodic meter reading for allocation month May, and so on\n\nThe expected meter reading for 01(05) is determined based on the demand with the same allocation month from the period of the\nprevious year 1(05) = 120 kW\n\nThe expected meter reading result is 120 kW .\n\nExample 6:Forecasts from the period of the previous year and changes to period\ndemand in the base period\n\n[J }--\u2014\u2014\u2014_}- |---|\n\n1.1.96 4.1.96           12.1.96 4.1.97     5.1.97\nMR Result 100        120         200      2 kW\ncoon J $$ pnannnnnnnnnfennnnnn | |---\nMR Reas. _\u2014\u2014P(4)        P(5) P(12)  P(4)       P(5)\n01(04)       01(05)   01(12)   01(04)      01(05)\n100       150                       kW/Year\nPerDem._ |]\n5.1.96\n\nPeriod demand was changed in the period 01(05) to 01(04). This change does not, however, influence extrapolation for time\n01(05) (5.1.97), because a change in period demand only influences the forecast period that follows directly after.\n\nThe expected meter reading for P(5) is determined based on the demand with the same allocation month from the period of the\nprevious year (P(5) = 120 kW)\n\nThe expected meter reading result is 120 kW .\n\nExample 7:Forecasts from period of the previous year and changes to period\ndemand in the previous year but not in the base period\n\n1.1.96 4.1.96              12.1.96 4.1.97       5.1.97\nMR Result       100               120                 200                2 kW\n-------- |\u2014\u2014______|------------|-----------| -\u2014_____|-----\nMR Reas.        P(4)              P(5) P12) P(4)            P(5)\n01(04)             01(05)  01(12) \u2014 01(04)           01(05)\n100                             150                         kW/Year\n\nPerDem,. |\u2014\u2014\u2014__|\n11.1.96\n",
